  'matric-celebration-patrols-beaches-long-street-2026-11-20',
  'City steps up beach and Long Street patrols as matrics finish exams',
  'Community', '2026-11-20', 'Cape Times', 'https://capetimes.co.za/news/2026-11-20-cape-town-steps-up-beach-and-long-street-patrols-as-matric-celebrations-begin/',
  'The City of Cape Town is putting more patrols, checkpoints and roadblocks at beaches, the CBD and Long Street as matrics celebrate the end of their final exams.',
  'The City of Cape Town says its enforcement agencies will be more visible at beaches, in the Central Business District and along Long Street as matric learners celebrate the end of their final exam papers. The announcement came ahead of the last papers on Friday, 20 November.

According to the City, foot and vehicle patrols will be backed by targeted vehicle checkpoints and roadblocks. Thousands of matriculants are expected at beaches, bars and nightlife spots once their exams are over.

Under City by-laws, nobody may carry or drink alcohol out in the open, whether on a beach, in a park or on the street. The City says officers will take a zero-tolerance approach: anyone caught transporting or drinking alcohol in public will have it confiscated and face an immediate R500 fine.

The City advises matriculants to arrange safe transport, such as a designated driver, to tell their parents where they are going and to keep their phones charged with enough airtime or data to call for help. Learners are also urged to store 021 480 7700, the number for the City''s emergency communication centre, in their phones.',
  NULL, NULL, NULL,
